1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
Hey friends and welcome to the Riker Medical Podcast.

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:09,720
Riker Medical is a platform for education focused on emergency, transport, and critical

3
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:15,360
care medicine.

4
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:20,440
We believe that the sharing of knowledge should be free, accessible to all, and that innovative

5
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:23,960
use of technology can facilitate that effort.

6
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:29,960
This podcast is just one piece of that whole project.

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:37,040
Also, while we may mention medical treatments and interventions along the way, remember

8
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:40,800
that we are just strangers on the internet and don't do things you aren't allowed to

9
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,800
do.

10
00:00:43,800 --> 00:01:11,800
For more information about the project, visit us at RikerMedical.com.

11
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:20,080
In this introductory episode of the podcast, we just want to take some time to explain

12
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:23,200
what's going on here at Riker Medical.

13
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:26,040
We'll start with a review of how we got here.

14
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:30,760
We'll explain where things are at and how this podcast fits into the picture.

15
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:35,080
We'll paint a vision of what we hope this project to become and then we'll end it with

16
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:40,080
a discussion about how you can get involved.

17
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:45,320
Riker Medical started with a book on ventilator management for pre-hospital folks.

18
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:49,640
We self-published that resource to help clinicians in the field gain a basic understanding of

19
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,760
ventilators and transport.

20
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:56,040
The idea from the beginning was to make that a free resource for everyone.

21
00:01:56,040 --> 00:02:00,800
We got set up as an LLC and started the webpage to have a place to host it.

22
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,600
You can access and download that book for free.

23
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:10,440
Just head over to RikerMedical.com and navigate to this section on vent management.

24
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:15,280
Once we had the website started, we slowly began to add other bits of content there,

25
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:18,280
various resources for clinicians in the field.

26
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:23,600
We've got some drug references, examples of protocols, cheat sheets, that sort of thing.

27
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:28,320
There's lots more in the works, but it takes time and we got distracted by another idea

28
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,720
that brought us to where we are now.

29
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:35,040
The thought struck us that there are lots of people out there working in the field that

30
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:40,240
have insight to offer, but there's not a good way for those motivated individuals to share

31
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:44,040
what they know without a lot of upfront effort to make it happen.

32
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:48,480
Our vent book, for example, has been out for over a year now and the reach we've been able

33
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,760
to achieve is pretty limited.

34
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:55,200
That seems unfortunate as we imagine there are great many medics and nurses out there

35
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:58,560
who would be stoked to come across this type of thing.

36
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:03,920
Our solution for that is to try and use this platform, which is slowly gaining attention,

37
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:08,800
to allow others to publicize what they have to offer to the greater community.

38
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:13,440
Taking that idea one step further, we thought it'd be pretty rad to make it happen via a

39
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,960
continuing education exchange.

40
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:21,400
We could build out a CE program to give hours back to people who contribute their work.

41
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:27,040
The idea is to foster some sense of community that both provides valuable content and gives

42
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,680
a benefit back to those who do the work.

43
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,440
Of course, we want the thing to be free.

44
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:37,580
Now if you follow us on social media, you may already know that we did get granted organizational

45
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:41,000
accreditation for a CE program through CAPSIE.

46
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,600
That's the Commission on Accreditation for Pre-Hospital Continuing Education.

47
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:49,920
Unfortunately and for a variety of reasons that we don't need to get into, CAPSIE has

48
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:54,600
revoked that accreditation until we add a few more pieces to the puzzle and resubmit

49
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,600
our application.

50
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:59,080
That's where we're at for now.

51
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:03,160
This podcast will eventually be part of that CE program.

52
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:06,280
Listeners will be able to pitch ideas to us for episodes.

53
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:12,040
We will work with them to make it happen and then CE credit will be awarded in the exchange.

54
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:16,560
In addition, there will be an option for the community at large to get credit for listening

55
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:21,840
to certain episodes and taking quizzes or some sort of competency assessment that accompany

56
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:23,520
those episodes.

57
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:27,480
For now, we don't have the capacity to award credit, but we are still looking for content

58
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:32,680
contributors to work with us through the process so that we can demonstrate to CAPSIE exactly

59
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:37,440
how the quality control aspects work on our end.

60
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:41,360
So if you're interested in that sort of thing, here's how it would happen.

61
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:46,840
Head on over to rightgormedical.com, follow the links to the ConEd program development

62
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:50,520
page and submit an activity application.

63
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:54,880
You will review that application and then get back to you on next steps for making it

64
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,160
happen.

65
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:01,240
In the meantime, we here at Riker Medical have a few ideas for episodes and will try

66
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,360
to contribute regularly to the show.

67
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:07,760
Now, it is worth noting that not all of the stuff we host on the show or on the website

68
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:09,880
fall into the CE program.

69
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:14,680
We may choose to share things that are non-clinical or otherwise non-testable and therefore can't

70
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:18,000
really be worked into the continuing education side of things.

71
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,320
So the show will be a mix of both.

72
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,920
That said, if you have an idea for an episode that probably won't meet criteria for the

73
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:27,160
CE program, we're also game for that as well.

74
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:32,500
You can use the very same application to get in touch and we'll take it from there.

75
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:38,440
As far as what sorts of things fall into the CE model, that takes a bit of explaining.

76
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:42,720
Our initial pitch to CAPSIE included seven activities.

77
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:46,040
First are the podcast and blog, which are pretty self-explanatory.

78
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:50,040
We'd give credit to folks for contributing episodes or posts.

79
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:54,400
We also envisioned a mentorship activity in which we could give credit to an experienced

80
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:59,480
clinician for building out a mentorship program for someone new to the field or with less

81
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,480
experience.

82
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:05,960
Then there was the idea of annotated illustrations, offering credit for explaining concepts visually

83
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:06,960
or graphically.

84
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:11,880
We also had a reflection activity in which someone could share an experience via the

85
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:17,880
platform in an active reflection or debrief, whether that be text, audio, or video.

86
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:22,040
Another idea was the critique, essentially a way for someone to informally peer-reviewed

87
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:26,440
content produced by someone else and to provide constructive feedback on whatever it might

88
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,440
be.

89
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:32,120
Lastly, was the instructional design activity in which we give credit to people for building

90
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,800
out courses or lessons.

91
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:39,360
The hope moving forward is to find a way to make all of these activities work.

92
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:43,960
The catch is that we now also have to have a mechanism to offer the community at large

93
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:49,600
the opportunity to earn credit for participating in or consuming whatever content we put out

94
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:52,200
through the CE program.

95
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:56,520
Just to be clear, this is at the request of CAPSIE as the accrediting body, so there's

96
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,800
no real workaround for us there.

97
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:04,480
The plan is to get content up on a learning management system or LMS so that anyone can

98
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:10,160
access those final projects and participate in them for credit, which is cool.

99
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:14,480
That means that we'll eventually have a library of stuff to meet whatever CE needs you might

100
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,440
have.

101
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:21,060
The downside or the problem to be overcome is that not all of these activities we initially

102
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:23,580
envisioned are readily testable.

103
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:28,520
So let's say you want to do a reflection on a run you had and how it affected you personally.

104
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:32,400
That's not something that lends itself to educational goals or learning outcomes that

105
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:37,360
we could put down on a lesson plan for others to get credit from, which is totally okay

106
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:39,640
and we're still down to host your story.

107
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:43,680
It just means that we've got to sort out which contributions will be part of the CE

108
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:47,480
program and which will be just for the sake of getting it out there into the universe

109
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:50,560
and sharing the experience.

110
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:54,000
Another problematic example is the mentorship program.

111
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:59,120
It's a bit tough to test outsiders on a one-on-one mentorship session.

112
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:04,740
That said, we can work to design those plans to focus on specific goals or objectives.

113
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:10,660
We could then record those sessions and share via the LMS like any other asynchronous course.

114
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:15,380
In fact, there's also the option to live stream them so that participants can get credit

115
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:16,900
in real time.

116
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:21,620
In that scenario, we'd be able to give credit to the mentor for developing and guiding the

117
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:27,140
session, to the live audience for participating synchronously, and then to the stragglers

118
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:31,180
who watch it asynchronously via the LMS.

119
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:35,300
We've been toying with this idea along with some of our partners, so more on that whenever

120
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:37,180
we get it worked out.

121
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:41,620
But to summarize where things are at currently, we're going to make this CE program happen

122
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:45,180
one way or another and when we do, it'll be badass.

123
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:49,460
In the meantime, we'll work on getting this podcast and the blog going and are open to

124
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:52,180
any help we can get.

125
00:08:52,180 --> 00:08:56,940
The end goal or vision for it all is that we will exist as a home for high-quality learning

126
00:08:56,940 --> 00:09:01,500
opportunities created for and by a community of clinicians.

127
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:05,860
We can help hash out ideas and refine projects to meet industry standards and requirements

128
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:10,700
of accreditation, but our hope is to eventually become a host and let you guys keep the things

129
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,940
going.

130
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:16,740
We're here to get it all started, to do the logistics and maintain accreditation, and

131
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:19,620
then we'll probably still want to pitch in every now and again with new thoughts and

132
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:21,660
ideas as they come up.

133
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:26,860
Basically, we want to break the mold that keeps ground-level providers from pitching

134
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:29,340
in on the full-med community.

135
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:34,380
Lots of folks have stuff to offer, but not everyone has an in to make it happen.

136
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:38,480
And then oftentimes it's the case that someone has an idea in the works, but not a good way

137
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:41,580
to collaborate on and develop that idea.

138
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:44,700
That for sure was the case when we put the vent book together.

139
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:49,180
There wasn't an established mechanism to work with peers on those ideas.

140
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:53,220
Hopefully, Reicher Medical can be that supportive community for others.

141
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:58,900
We want to both give clinicians a way to contribute and support them in that effort via constructive

142
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:01,620
and cooperative approach.

143
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:06,380
And then to take that concept just a bit further, we're hoping to make the CE program as affordable

144
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:07,900
as possible.

145
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:12,420
The content development side of the house will for sure be put out for free, and all

146
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:16,940
the things we create will be openly available to anyone with a computer.

147
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:21,140
We're going to try and make the CEs that go with those things free also, but that's

148
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:23,720
dependent on a handful of factors.

149
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:29,460
So it might end up just being ridiculously cheap until we can get funding worked out.

150
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:32,300
And then there's one other part of the vision.

151
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:37,020
CAPSI is the accrediting body for EMS stuff, and that's where we're starting.

152
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:41,220
But there are also avenues to get CEs for our nursing colleagues, and there are specialty

153
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:44,780
boards that many of us use for maintenance of certifications.

154
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:49,460
We'll get there eventually, but for now it's one step at a time.

155
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:51,180
So that's the general idea.

156
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:56,100
Now you know how we got here, where things are at with us, and what we're hoping to make

157
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,340
happen.

158
00:10:57,340 --> 00:10:59,620
Next step is how you can get involved.

159
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,780
First and foremost, check out the website.

160
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:06,420
You can always get in touch with us there, or on social media, or by adding comments

161
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:09,180
here, wherever you happen to be listening to this.

162
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:13,220
We are open to any and all ideas or suggestions.

163
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:17,860
But more specifically, we need to get some content up in order to resubmit our application

164
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:18,860
at CAPSI.

165
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:24,220
We've got details about that on the website, but we need examples of each of the activities

166
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:28,660
we want to include in the program, and the more the merrier.

167
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:33,220
So if any of them sound appealing to you, hit us up and we can make it happen.

168
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:38,220
We also need help figuring out exactly how to host all the things and track users in

169
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,540
the system.

170
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:43,300
So if you have experience working with the LMS side of things and want to share what

171
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:46,820
you know, we could use some help there too.

172
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:51,600
And then lastly, we also need people to lend a hand as content reviewers.

173
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:56,020
As activities get rolling, we have a cadre of volunteers that maintain a dialogue with

174
00:11:56,020 --> 00:12:01,380
participants to offer feedback and guidance as the projects start to take form.

175
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:06,180
And then once submitted, we review them internally to make sure everything is copacetic and meets

176
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,380
all the standards we are held to.

177
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:12,300
If that sounds like something you're into, just let us know and we can set up a time

178
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:15,000
to discuss.

179
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,660
And that's pretty much it.

180
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:18,060
Thanks for tuning in.

181
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:21,860
But real quick before we go, just a few shout outs.

182
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:26,940
First is to Pragmatic Paramedics, another awesome podcast that we highly recommend.

183
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:30,260
Next is to the St. Fisher Church of Evidence-Based Medicine.

184
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:33,500
If you don't follow them already, definitely check them out.

185
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:38,280
These guys, both Pragmatic Paramedics and the St. Fisher folks, have been instrumental

186
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:42,140
in getting our stuff out there into the world and we truly appreciate that.

187
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:46,060
And then we'll end things with a shout out to my good friend Josh Pittman and his buddy

188
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:47,540
Kevin Pons.

189
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:49,700
They put the music together for the show.

190
00:12:49,700 --> 00:13:02,620
Until next time.
